 ],
 "notes": "Scope: I indexed texts 1 and 2 only, as the task asked. I read all three texts in full and changed no project files. I tested every pattern with a word-start scanner over these units: (a) Zacher chapters (Latin, RU, EN and the parallel chips) and notes (RU, EN, source); (b) the Odyssey page's s1–s4, the margin notes and the s3 review log; (c) the study's abstract, sections, footnotes and appendix blocks, which use the same pattern set. Hits per entity (units): Julius Valerius 93 (zacher only; the chapter hits come from the 'Юлий Валерий 1,N' chips); Pseudo-Callisthenes 56 (chips plus 'Ps.-Call.' in source lines; the note bodies only say 'α'); epitomator 30; Plutarch 5; Diodorus 7 (zacher n42, n44, n52; odyssey n1b, n2b); Herodotus 1; Arrian 5; Pliny 1; Clitarchus 1; Memnon 1; Photius 1; Pausanias 1 (n71 only: the pattern needs a following numeral, so Pausanias of Orestis in c24, n43, n44 is not hit); Vincent 1; Favorinus 1; Homer 16 (odyssey s2, s3, n2a, n3a and the study); Thucydides 3; Eratosthenes 4; Strabo 12; Asclepiades 3; Tzetzes 3 (including the s2 chip 'поздний слой: P, Цец'); Lycophron 2; Pindar 4; Aristarchus 17; Palaephatus 2. I found no false hits. LOCI CONVENTIONS: (1) The chapter parallel chips are shown on the page in each chapter head, so I indexed them as loci at c<N>/'I.<N>'. The chips 'у Юлия Валерия не сохранилось' (ch. 1–3) cite no passage and are skipped. The ch. 46 chip '1.46 and 1.46a' is given as 1.46–46a. (2) In each note, the body and the source line are merged and deduplicated. Where the source line is fuller I used it: Paus. 6.15.3–5 (the body has 6,15,3) and Iul. Val. 1.42–45 (the body has 'гл. 43–45 по Мюллеру'). (3) locus '' means the work is cited without a passage number: β in n1, n4, n11, n24, n39; the Armenian version in n1, n13; α in n4, n25; Iul. Val. in n1, n27, n31, n59 (readings of its manuscripts T, P and the Milan codex); Tragodoumena in n2a. (4) Other loci as cited: PGM 'IV.154–285' and 'IV.296–466'; Phot. Bibl. 'cod. 224'; Armenian version '§ 31' (Venice 1842, p. 16); Iul. Val. '1.31–33' in n50 follows Müller's chapter numbers. Edition page citations (Kübler, Kroll, Zacher, Müller pages) are not loci. (5) Odyssey page: each scholion segment s1–s4 is indexed twice, as Hom. Od. 10.N (the lemma it quotes) and as schol-od 10.N (the scholion itself, author 'anon'). The Pindar quotation in s3 is entered as fr. 33d, the number n3a gives it. The section heading 'Гомер, «Одиссея» 10.1–4' has no anchor in the scheme and is not indexed. Review logs are not indexed. (6) Labels for Odyssey notes are 'прим. 1a', 'прим. 1b', 'прим. 2a', 'прим. 2b', 'прим. 3a', 'прим. 3b', 'прим. 4a' (I read '<id>' as the anchor without 'n'). The marks shown on the page are Greek letters: n1a=α, n1b=β, n2a=γ, n2b=δ, n3a=ε, n3b=ϛ, n4a=ζ. Relabel to 'прим. α' etc. if wanted. EXCLUDED: characters who are not cited as authors (Aristotle and Anaximenes as Alexander's teachers, the diviners Antiphon and Aristander, the athlete Clitomachus); modern scholars and editors (Kübler, Kroll, Zacher, Müller, Mai, Ausfeld, Preisendanz, Dindorf, Buttmann, Pontani, Snell–Maehler); internal cross-references to other chapters of the Epitome (no work record is made for the Epitome itself; its anonymous compiler is the 'epitomator' author). Clitarchus, Memnon, Eratosthenes, Vincent of Beauvais, Favorinus, Lycophron and Palaephatus are named without a work or passage, so they have author records but no works. 'anon' is used as author_id for PGM and the Odyssey scholia and has no author record. WIKIDATA: every Q-id was found with wbsearchentities and checked with wbgetentities (label and description). The α and β recensions, the Odyssey scholia, the Tragodoumena, Tzetzes' commentary on Lycophron and Pindar's fragments have no confirmed item and are left ''. Q974482 (Alexander Romance as a whole) was not used for the recensions. No places, so pleiades is '' throughout. The working files (pattern tester, loci builder, final.json) are in C:/Users/user/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--Users-user-Documents-Projects-Neoscholia/b4f946bd-6075-477c-b48c-f9c5ba60c113/scratchpad/."
